We complete the square in $x$ and $y$ to get the equation of the ellipse in standard form. We have
\begin{align*} 4x^2 - 8x + y^2 + 4y - 8 &= 0 \\ 4(x^2 - 2x) + (y^2 + 4y) - 8 &= 0 \\ 4(x^2 - 2x + 1) + (y^2 + 4y + 4) - 8 - 4 - 4 &= 0 \\ 4(x - 1)^2 + (y + 2)^2 &= 16 \\ \frac{(x - 1)^2}{4} + \frac{(y + 2)^2}{16} &= 1 \end{align*}
This is the equation of an ellipse centered at $(1,-2).$  Here, $a^2 = 16,$ so $a = 4,$ and $b^2 = 4,$ so $b = 2.$  Also, $c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 16 - 4 = 12,$ so $c = \sqrt{12} = 2 \sqrt{3}.$

